1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:08,251
Before your feet hit the floor this morning, the math had already started.

2
00:00:08,732 --> 00:00:09,799
What's due.

3
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,710
What's in the account.

4
00:00:12,191 --> 00:00:14,431
What happens if the hours get cut.

5
00:00:14,913 --> 00:00:19,115
Some of you did that math at three in the morning, staring at the ceiling.

6
00:00:20,568 --> 00:00:22,338
Give me the next ten minutes.

7
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:27,287
There's one line in the prayer Jesus taught that speaks straight to that,

8
00:00:27,287 --> 00:00:29,796
and most of us say it without hearing it.

9
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:36,389
In Luke chapter eleven, one of the disciples says, Lord, teach us to pray.

10
00:00:36,871 --> 00:00:40,668
And in Matthew chapter six, Jesus lays the prayer out.

11
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:42,942
Verses nine through eleven.

12
00:00:44,844 --> 00:00:49,646
After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven,

13
00:00:49,646 --> 00:00:54,307
Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth,

14
00:00:54,307 --> 00:00:58,049
as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread.

15
00:00:59,913 --> 00:01:01,492
Look where the bread sits.

16
00:01:01,973 --> 00:01:05,365
Right after, Thy kingdom come, and Thy will be done.

17
00:01:05,847 --> 00:01:09,516
The God who runs heaven wants to hear about your groceries.

18
00:01:11,668 --> 00:01:14,484
Some people think that's too small to pray about.

19
00:01:14,966 --> 00:01:20,790
God has wars and hospitals to see about, so why would He care about my light bill?

20
00:01:21,271 --> 00:01:24,002
Jesus answered that in the same chapter.

21
00:01:24,484 --> 00:01:26,702
Matthew six, verse twenty-six.

22
00:01:28,605 --> 00:01:33,234
Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap,

23
00:01:33,234 --> 00:01:39,293
nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye not much better than

24
00:01:39,293 --> 00:01:39,634
they?

25
00:01:41,498 --> 00:01:45,466
He feeds birds, and He says you are worth more than they are.

26
00:01:45,947 --> 00:01:47,739
Peter put it in one line.

27
00:01:48,221 --> 00:01:50,887
First Peter chapter five, verse seven.

28
00:01:52,790 --> 00:01:56,630
Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.

29
00:01:58,494 --> 00:01:59,774
All your care.

30
00:02:00,255 --> 00:02:01,578
The rent counts.

31
00:02:02,059 --> 00:02:06,411
So does the tire that's going bald, and the child who needs shoes.

32
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:09,943
If it's on your mind, it's allowed in your prayer.

33
00:02:12,096 --> 00:02:14,933
Now a working person pushes back right here.

34
00:02:15,415 --> 00:02:17,399
Nobody handed me anything.

35
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,139
I clock in.

36
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,263
I earn what I've got.

37
00:02:21,744 --> 00:02:23,494
And you do work hard.

38
00:02:23,975 --> 00:02:27,367
But Moses warned Israel about that exact thought.

39
00:02:27,849 --> 00:02:31,774
Deuteronomy chapter eight, verses seventeen and eighteen.

40
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:35,602
And thou say in thine heart,

41
00:02:35,602 --> 00:02:41,583
My power and the might of mine hand hath gotten me this wealth. But thou shalt remember

42
00:02:41,583 --> 00:02:46,259
the LORD thy God: for it is he that giveth thee power to get wealth,

43
00:02:46,259 --> 00:02:52,172
that he may establish his covenant which he sware unto thy fathers, as it is this day.

44
00:02:54,036 --> 00:02:56,276
The strength in your back is from Him.

45
00:02:56,758 --> 00:02:59,080
So is the mind that learned the trade,

46
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,198
and the breath you took on the way in this morning.

47
00:03:02,679 --> 00:03:05,004
Paul told the men of Athens the same.

48
00:03:05,486 --> 00:03:08,558
Acts chapter seventeen, verse twenty-five.

49
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:14,976
Neither is worshipped with men's hands, as though he needed any thing,

50
00:03:14,976 --> 00:03:18,652
seeing he giveth to all life, and breath, and all things;

51
00:03:20,516 --> 00:03:23,503
And the food came out of ground you didn't make.

52
00:03:23,984 --> 00:03:26,800
Psalm one hundred four, verse fourteen.

53
00:03:28,703 --> 00:03:31,610
He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle,

54
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:36,831
and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;

55
00:03:38,694 --> 00:03:40,998
The check has your employer's name on it.

56
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,720
It came from higher up than that.

57
00:03:45,872 --> 00:03:48,176
Now notice what Jesus asked for.

58
00:03:48,658 --> 00:03:49,618
This day.

59
00:03:50,099 --> 00:03:53,619
He didn't ask for the month, or enough to retire on.

60
00:03:54,101 --> 00:03:55,978
That goes back to the wilderness.

61
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:59,254
Israel is hungry, and God answers.

62
00:03:59,736 --> 00:04:02,552
Exodus chapter sixteen, verse four.

63
00:04:04,454 --> 00:04:07,005
Then said the LORD unto Moses, Behold,

64
00:04:07,005 --> 00:04:12,846
I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain

65
00:04:12,846 --> 00:04:18,150
rate every day, that I may prove them, whether they will walk in my law, or no.

66
00:04:20,014 --> 00:04:21,145
Every day.

67
00:04:21,626 --> 00:04:25,146
Some of them kept extra for the morning, just in case.

68
00:04:25,628 --> 00:04:28,721
By sunrise it had worms in it, and it stank.

69
00:04:29,202 --> 00:04:31,058
God wasn't being stingy.

70
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:35,060
He was teaching a whole nation to look up every morning.

71
00:04:36,512 --> 00:04:38,837
Jesus said the same about worry.

72
00:04:39,319 --> 00:04:42,284
Matthew chapter six, verse thirty-four.

73
00:04:44,187 --> 00:04:49,413
Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the

74
00:04:49,413 --> 00:04:53,317
things of itself. Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.

75
00:04:55,881 --> 00:04:57,929
There's nothing wrong with saving.

76
00:04:58,411 --> 00:05:01,675
Proverbs praises the ant for storing up in the summer.

77
00:05:02,156 --> 00:05:05,591
The trouble starts when the savings become the thing you trust.

78
00:05:06,072 --> 00:05:09,351
Jesus told about a man whose barns were so full,

79
00:05:09,351 --> 00:05:12,494
he planned to tear them down and build bigger.

80
00:05:12,975 --> 00:05:15,364
Luke chapter twelve, verse twenty.

81
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:19,557
But God said unto him, Thou fool,

82
00:05:19,557 --> 00:05:25,110
this night thy soul shall be required of thee: then whose shall those things be,

83
00:05:25,110 --> 00:05:26,845
which thou hast provided?

84
00:05:28,709 --> 00:05:29,755
One night.

85
00:05:30,236 --> 00:05:32,391
A job can go in one meeting.

86
00:05:32,872 --> 00:05:35,176
A house can go in one storm.

87
00:05:35,658 --> 00:05:38,175
Paul told Timothy where to put the weight.

88
00:05:38,657 --> 00:05:41,835
First Timothy chapter six, verse seventeen.

89
00:05:43,737 --> 00:05:48,768
Charge them that are rich in this world, that they be not highminded,

90
00:05:48,768 --> 00:05:52,631
nor trust in uncertain riches, but in the living God,

91
00:05:52,631 --> 00:05:55,620
who giveth us richly all things to enjoy;

92
00:05:57,484 --> 00:06:00,236
Uncertain riches, or the living God.

93
00:06:00,718 --> 00:06:03,427
Every morning you pick one to stand on.

94
00:06:05,579 --> 00:06:08,054
So what does it look like to live that way?

95
00:06:08,535 --> 00:06:12,866
Go to a widow in a town called Zarephath, in the middle of a famine.

96
00:06:13,347 --> 00:06:16,270
She has a handful of meal and a little oil.

97
00:06:16,752 --> 00:06:19,098
One last meal for her and her son.

98
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:23,889
Elijah asks her to make him a cake first, and gives her this word.

99
00:06:24,371 --> 00:06:27,549
First Kings chapter seventeen, verse fourteen.

100
00:06:29,452 --> 00:06:34,673
For thus saith the LORD God of Israel, The barrel of meal shall not waste,

101
00:06:34,673 --> 00:06:37,213
neither shall the cruse of oil fail,

102
00:06:37,213 --> 00:06:41,164
until the day that the LORD sendeth rain upon the earth.

103
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:44,094
She did it.

104
00:06:44,576 --> 00:06:47,370
And the Bible doesn't say her barrel filled up.

105
00:06:47,852 --> 00:06:49,772
It says it did not run out.

106
00:06:50,253 --> 00:06:53,496
Day after day she went back to it, and there was enough.

107
00:06:54,948 --> 00:06:56,378
That's daily bread.

108
00:06:56,859 --> 00:06:59,078
David watched it his whole life.

109
00:06:59,559 --> 00:07:02,311
Psalm thirty-seven, verse twenty-five.

110
00:07:04,213 --> 00:07:09,713
I have been young, and now am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken,

111
00:07:09,713 --> 00:07:11,616
nor his seed begging bread.

112
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:18,809
And if you wonder whether God is willing, go up a mountain with Abraham.

113
00:07:19,291 --> 00:07:21,787
His son asks him, where is the lamb?

114
00:07:22,268 --> 00:07:25,106
Genesis chapter twenty-two, verse eight.

115
00:07:27,008 --> 00:07:28,790
And Abraham said, My son,

116
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:35,136
God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.

117
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,536
God did provide.

118
00:07:39,017 --> 00:07:40,937
A ram, caught in a thicket.

119
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:44,661
And Abraham named that place Jehovah-jireh.

120
00:07:45,143 --> 00:07:49,324
Many centuries later, God provided the Lamb, His own Son.

121
00:07:49,806 --> 00:07:52,536
So Paul asks the question that settles it.

122
00:07:53,018 --> 00:07:55,727
Romans chapter eight, verse thirty-two.

123
00:07:57,630 --> 00:08:02,019
He that spared not his own Son, but delivered him up for us all,

124
00:08:02,019 --> 00:08:05,928
how shall he not with him also freely give us all things?

125
00:08:07,792 --> 00:08:11,845
If He gave you Jesus, He is not going to hold back bread.

126
00:08:12,327 --> 00:08:15,164
And Jesus said something more about bread.

127
00:08:15,646 --> 00:08:18,483
John chapter six, verse thirty-five.

128
00:08:20,385 --> 00:08:22,080
And Jesus said unto them,

129
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:28,111
I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on

130
00:08:28,111 --> 00:08:29,601
me shall never thirst.

131
00:08:31,465 --> 00:08:35,647
The deepest hunger you have, a paycheck was never going to fill.

132
00:08:37,799 --> 00:08:39,250
So here's today.

133
00:08:39,731 --> 00:08:44,104
Before you ask for anything, thank Him for what's already on the table.

134
00:08:44,586 --> 00:08:46,847
Psalm sixty-eight, verse nineteen.

135
00:08:48,749 --> 00:08:52,912
Blessed be the Lord, who daily loadeth us with benefits,

136
00:08:52,912 --> 00:08:55,661
even the God of our salvation. Selah.

137
00:08:57,525 --> 00:08:58,400
Daily.

138
00:08:58,882 --> 00:09:03,255
Then tell Him what you need, by name, the way a child asks a father.

139
00:09:03,736 --> 00:09:06,979
And then go to work, and leave tomorrow where it is.

140
00:09:08,431 --> 00:09:10,373
Let's pray together this morning.

141
00:09:10,854 --> 00:09:13,755
Father, in the name of Jesus, we come to You.

142
00:09:14,237 --> 00:09:17,855
Thank You for breath this morning, for strength to work,

143
00:09:17,855 --> 00:09:20,957
and for every meal we never had to wonder about.

144
00:09:21,438 --> 00:09:25,022
Forgive us for the days we thought our own hands did it.

145
00:09:25,504 --> 00:09:29,003
You know what's due this week, and You know what's in the account.

146
00:09:29,484 --> 00:09:31,703
Give us this day our daily bread.

147
00:09:32,184 --> 00:09:36,131
Teach us to trust You for today, and to leave tomorrow with You.

148
00:09:36,612 --> 00:09:39,514
And thank You for Jesus, the bread of life.

149
00:09:39,995 --> 00:09:42,129
In Jesus' name, amen.

150
00:09:43,581 --> 00:09:48,680
If you prayed that with me, type amen, and send this to a friend who needs it.

151
00:09:49,161 --> 00:09:50,420
One more thing.

152
00:09:50,901 --> 00:09:54,699
Tonight at eight thirty Eastern, come back for the night prayer.

153
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,356
Tonight it's called, Lay It Down.

154
00:09:57,838 --> 00:09:59,224
Have a blessed day.

